From: Joseph Telaak <joseph@telaak.dev>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 17:51:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] sf_smac: do not advertise VHT on 2.4 GHz

siwifi_set_vht_capa() sets vht_supported on every band of the wiphy,
2.4 GHz included. The 2.4 GHz radio of the SF19A2890 is an 802.11n
radio. VHT there is only the non-standard "256-QAM on 2.4 GHz"
extension, which hostapd runs as vendor_vht. OpenWrt's wifi-scripts
then configure the 2.4 GHz radio as VHT20 instead of HT20/HT40.

Advertise VHT on 5 GHz only. The 2.4 GHz radio then reports plain HT,
and the firmware's ME configuration gets vht_supp = 0 for it.

Signed-off-by: Joseph Telaak <joseph@telaak.dev>
---
 sf_smac/src/bb_src/umac/siwifi_mod_params.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/sf_smac/src/bb_src/umac/siwifi_mod_params.c
+++ b/sf_smac/src/bb_src/umac/siwifi_mod_params.c
@@ -310,6 +310,9 @@ void siwifi_set_vht_capa(struct siwifi_h
         return;
     for (band = NL80211_BAND_2GHZ; band <= NL80211_BAND_5GHZ; band++) {
         struct ieee80211_sta_vht_cap *vht_cap = NULL;
+        /* VHT is a 5 GHz PHY; the 2.4 GHz radio is 802.11n */
+        if (band == NL80211_BAND_2GHZ)
+            continue;
         if(wiphy->bands[band] != NULL) {
             vht_cap = &wiphy->bands[band]->vht_cap;
         }
